Compiled artifacts are looked up by sha256 of the module uri, and a
file-locator's uri is its realpath'd absolute path. Artifacts compiled in
one tree are therefore never found when the package is loaded from another
path, so --compiled-read-only-dir misses for anything shipped as a package.

Instead, key files inside an npm package by npm://<pkg>/<path-in-package>:
module-finder records the package directory and uri prefix (LogicalRoot)
when it enters a package via an npm() import, and locators for files under
that directory get uri() overridden accordingly. url-file already overrides
uri() the same way for locally-cached urls.

